<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Decomposition of Accelerator Topology</h3>

<section id="S3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.1 </span>Ring Datapath Definition</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We define a ring datapath based on the formulation of the accelerator topology as a directed graph. Consider a set of accelerators denoted as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=\{R_{0},R_{1},\dots,R_{n-1}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=\{R_{0},R_{1},\dots,R_{n-1}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th rank in the communication group. Each accelerator <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> has several communication ports that can be connected to other accelerators via electrical or fiber-optic cables and optionally a set of network switches. Due to duplex communication mode, a cable <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> connecting <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> establishes two logical unidirectional communication links, denoted as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{i},R_{j},c_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{i},R_{j},c_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R_{j},R_{i},c_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R_{j},R_{i},c_{k})</annotation></semantics></math>. For accelerators interconnected via switches, there exist two communication links between each pair of accelerators but these links share the same amount of aggregated bandwidth.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">By treating the accelerators as vertices, the set of all unidirectional communication links forms a directed edge set by</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E1X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle E=\{(R_{i},R_{j},c_{k})\;\mid" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>∣</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle E=\{(R_{i},R_{j},c_{k})\;\mid</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{there exists a }\text{communication}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>there exists a </mtext><mtext>communication</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{there exists a }\text{communication}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E1Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{link from }R_{i}\text{ to }R_{j}\text{ via cable }c_{k}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>link from </mtext><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mtext> to </mtext><mi>R</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mtext> via cable </mtext><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{link from }R_{i}\text{ to }R_{j}\text{ via cable }c_{k}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Thus, the topology can be represented as a directed graph <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we define a ring datapath. A ring datapath on <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a subgraph <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subseteq G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subseteq G</annotation></semantics></math> that forms a directed Hamiltonian cycle, <span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">i.e.</span>, a directed cycle that visits every vertex in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> exactly once. Two ring datapaths <math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{i}=(V,E_{i}),D_{j}=(V,E_{j}),i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{i}=(V,E_{i}),D_{j}=(V,E_{j}),i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math> are said to be <span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">orthogonal ring datapaths</span> if they are edge-disjoint, that is,</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{i}\cap E_{j}=\emptyset." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{i}\cap E_{j}=\emptyset.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The property ensures that a set of mutually orthogonal ring datapaths can support simultaneous data transfer without mutual interference.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.2 </span>Single-Node topology Decomposition</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The most common topology in modern single-node accelerators is the AlltoAll topology, encompassing switch-based (NVIDIA GPUs) and full-mesh (AMD GPUs) ones.
Theoretically, both topologies can be represented as a complete directed graph <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> of degree <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>.
For decomposition of these AlltoAll topologies, we can directly apply the existing <em id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Hamiltonian decomposition of complete directed graphs into edge-disjoint Hamiltonian Cycles</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a>, <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>]</cite> (denoted in this paper as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>-decomposition).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in Figure <a href="#S3.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 3.1.2 Single-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we use 8 accelerators within a single node (<span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">i.e.</span>, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8}</annotation></semantics></math>) as an example, the decomposition scheme is computed via an algorithm demonstrated in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.1.2 Single-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> proposed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>, which decomposes a complete graph <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> within <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(n)</annotation></semantics></math> time complexity.
Based on this decomposition, the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times(n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times(n-1)</annotation></semantics></math> communication links are divided into a set of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> edge-disjoint Hamiltonian cycles. These cycles are then utilized as the mutually orthogonal ring datapaths for concurrent data transfer.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Decomposition of <math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}</annotation></semantics></math> into a set of Hamiltonian Cycles</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
                
                
               Integer <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\geq 8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\geq 8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\%4=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\%4=0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
                
                
               Hamiltonian cycle list <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\_cycles" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\_cycles</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
                
                
               // Generate Hamiltonian paths

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="init\_paths\leftarrow\textsc{GetPath}(n-2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GetPath</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">init\_paths\leftarrow\textsc{GetPath}(n-2)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
                
                
               // Link the paths to form cycles

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="init\_cycles\leftarrow\textsc{GenCycles}(init\_paths)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GenCycles</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">init\_cycles\leftarrow\textsc{GenCycles}(init\_paths)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
                
                
               // Find a set of edges in each cycle that forms a Hamiltonian Path

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow n/4-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow n/4-1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="shifts\leftarrow\{0:1,\,k+1:4k+2,\,2k+2:3,\,3k+2:4k\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 2</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn> 3</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">shifts\leftarrow\{0:1,\,k+1:4k+2,\,2k+2:3,\,3k+2:4k\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="shift\leftarrow shifts.get(i,2k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">shift\leftarrow shifts.get(i,2k)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rotated[i][j]\leftarrow init\_cycles[i][(j+shift)\%(n-1)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>%</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rotated[i][j]\leftarrow init\_cycles[i][(j+shift)\%(n-1)]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
                
                
               // Disconnect these edges to form paths

</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="appender[rotated[i][-1]]\leftarrow rotated[i][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">appender[rotated[i][-1]]\leftarrow rotated[i][0]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="appender\_list\leftarrow[n-2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">appender\_list\leftarrow[n-2]</annotation></semantics></math>, then append <math id="alg1.l12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="appender[last]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">appender[last]</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-2</annotation></semantics></math> steps

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
                
                
               // Link the paths to form cycles again

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
                
                
               <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\_cycles\leftarrow\textsc{GenCycles}(appender)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GenCycles</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\_cycles\leftarrow\textsc{GenCycles}(appender)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
                
                
               <span id="alg1.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\_cycles" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\_cycles</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.26541v1/decompose-K8.svg" id="S3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/118;" width="452" height="118"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Decomposition of 8-accelerator AlltoAll topology graph <math id="S3.F2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> into 7 edge-disjoint directed Hamiltonian cycles. The decomposed Hamiltonian cycles correspond to mutually orthogonal ring datapaths that traverse all 8 accelerators.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S3.F3" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.26541v1/multi-node.svg" id="S3.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:467/114;" width="467" height="114"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>Left: The 15 Hamiltonian cycles decomposed from the topology of H100-2 via a <math id="S3.F3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{16}-decomposition" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>16</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{16}-decomposition</annotation></semantics></math> scheme. Right: The 8 Hamilton cycles derived from a <math id="S3.F3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(8-K_{8}-8)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(8-K_{8}-8)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-decomposition scheme.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.1.3 </span>Multi-Node topology Decomposition</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In multi-node systems such as the NVIDIA DGX H100 GPU cluster <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>, multiple H100 servers each equipped with 8 H100 accelerators are inter-connected via a high-bandwidth Infiniband Network. Within each node, 8 accelerators are fully-connected via four ultra-high bandwidth NVSwitches, while at the same time, each accelerator is also connected with an IB NIC, making it possible for all 8 accelerators to independently and concurrently RDMA data over their own dedicated 400 Gb/s NIC.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To analyze the decomposition of such IB-connected multi-node accelerators, we first take a 2-node H100 cluster as an example (abbreviated as H100-2).
Since every two accelerators in H100-2 are either interconnected via ultra-high 7.2 TB/s (duplex) aggregated bandwidth NVLINK-based communication links or 800 GB/s (duplex) aggregated bandwidth IB-based communication links, we can simply model its topology as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8\times 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8\times 2}</annotation></semantics></math> and use the above mentioned <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{n}-decomposition" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{n}-decomposition</annotation></semantics></math> scheme for its topology decomposition, as illustrated in the left part of Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.1.2 Single-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, this decomposition scheme will result in under-utilization of the bandwidth of intra-node NVLINK-based communication links. In a <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8\times 2}-decomposition" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8\times 2}-decomposition</annotation></semantics></math> scheme there are <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\times 8=56" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times 8=56</annotation></semantics></math> communication links within each node whereas <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8\times 8=64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8\times 8=64</annotation></semantics></math> communication links from one node to the other. Consequently, each intra-node communication link will have a bandwidth of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7200/(56*2)\approx 64GB/s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>7200</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>56</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7200/(56*2)\approx 64GB/s</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas each inter-node communication link will have a bandwidth of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{800}{64*2}\approx 6.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>800</mn><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>6.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{800}{64*2}\approx 6.3</annotation></semantics></math> GB/s, an order of magnitude lower than the intra-node bandwidth. Consequently, the utilization of intra-node bandwidth is bounded by inter-node bandwidth.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To this end, we propose to model the topology of H100-2 as two <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> subgraphs inter-connected with 8 bidirectional or 16 unidirectional IB-based communication links (denoted as <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m-K_{m}-m)^{u}-decomposition" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>u</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m-K_{m}-m)^{u}-decomposition</annotation></semantics></math> where in this case <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=8</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=2</annotation></semantics></math>). This decomposition scheme is based on the Hamiltonian decomposition of each node into a set of <span id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Hamiltonian paths</span>. A Hamiltonian path is a path in a directed graph that visits each vertex exactly once.
As illustrated in the right part of Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.1.2 Single-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, the theoretical bandwidth of each unidirectional intra-node communication link (gray) are roughly 64 GB/s while the theoretical bandwidth of each unidirectional inter-node communication link (blue) are approximately 50 GB/s-only a 28% difference which is significantly smaller than the over 9x difference if <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8\times 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8\times 2}</annotation></semantics></math> decomposition is adopted.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we prove that the 2-node decomposition scheme can be generalized to an arbitrary <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u-node" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u-node</annotation></semantics></math> cluster.
If we decompose two <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8}</annotation></semantics></math> subgraphs into Hamiltonian paths, we can obtain 8 Hamiltonian cycles by connecting these paths end-to-end. Since the decomposed Hamiltonian paths are at the same time a row-complete Latin Square. In each row or column of a Latin Square the entries are mutually distinct. Consequently, all 8 accelerators will appear both at the start and the end of the decomposed Hamiltonian paths, utilizing all the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 8=16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 8=16</annotation></semantics></math> IB NICs. Moreover, through mathematical induction, it is provable that the above decomposition scheme can scale up to an arbitrary number of H100 nodes inter-connected via IB switches. Suppose we have already decomposed a <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-node cluster using the scheme, we can derive a decomposition of <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n+1</annotation></semantics></math>-node cluster simply by two steps (ranks denote accelerators): (1) dis-connect the communication links from <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank\;(8n-8)\sim(8n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank\;(8n-8)\sim(8n-1)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank\;0\sim 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank\;0\sim 7</annotation></semantics></math>; (2) connect <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank\;(8n-8)\sim(8n-1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank\;(8n-8)\sim(8n-1)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank\;(8n)\sim(8n+7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank\;(8n)\sim(8n+7)</annotation></semantics></math> and connect <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank\;(8n)\sim(8n+7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank\;(8n)\sim(8n+7)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="rank\;0\sim 7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn> 0</mn></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">rank\;0\sim 7</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Other topologies, such as hypercubes, can also be decomposed into orthogonal ring data-paths via Hamiltonian decomposition. However, due to space limitations and the growing architectural emphasis on AlltoAll connectivity, this paper focuses primarily on the single-node and multi-node AlltoAll topologies analyzed in this section.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.26541v1/Multi-Ring-AllGather.svg" id="S3.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:452/274;" width="452" height="274"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Top: The Ring AllGather communication primitive used in Ring Attention and its variants. Colored circles represent accelerators 0–7. Symbols <math id="S3.F4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t[0]\sim t[7]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t[0]\sim t[7]</annotation></semantics></math> denote the transferred KV blocks. Bottom: The Multi-Ring AllGather communication primitive designed for <math id="S3.F4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8}-decomposition" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8}-decomposition</annotation></semantics></math>. Each column illustrates one iteration with seven ring-styled data transfer for seven chunks of KV blocks. Symbol <math id="S3.F4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t[i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t[i,j]</annotation></semantics></math> represents the KV initially assigned at accelerator <math id="S3.F4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and circulates across all accelerators following the <math id="S3.F4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th ring-styled data transfer. Iterations 2–6 and ring-styled transfer 2-5 are omitted for brevity.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Decomposition of Ring AllGather</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.1 </span>Problem Definition.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For simplicity, we assume that for each query chunk, its Q tensors keep stationary and its KV tensors are sent to or received from other accelerators in a ring-style data transfer.
Based on the above assumption, the formulation of vanilla Ring Attention is composed of two separate components: a <span id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Ring AllGather Communication Primitive</span> that assigns a query chunk at each accelerator and one ring-styled data transfer pattern for sending and receiving these chunks, as well as a <span id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Chunk Placement Strategy</span> which defines the (initial) query chunk placement strategy on the accelerators.
Thus, given a Ring AllGather primitive and a Chunk Placement Strategy, the communication and computation of the vanilla Ring Attention scheme are well formulated and fully determined for every iteration.
As illustrated in Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.1.3 Multi-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, vanilla Ring Attention has three desirable properties.</p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Accessibility</span>: After <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> iterations of KV transfer and <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> iterations of Attention computation, every Q tensor can access every KV tensor (which are initially distributed among all accelerators) locally on its assigned accelerator.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Zero-copy</span>: No additional memory is consumed due to KV tensor duplication.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Load balance</span>: For bi-directional non-causal Attention, as long as the query chunks are distributed evenly among the accelerators, computation and memory load are balanced across all accelerators. For causal Attention, however, there are two types of workload balance methods, including Striped Attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> and Zig-zag Ring Attention <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The former two of the above properties correspond to the first component <span id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Ring AllGather Communication Primitive</span> of the vanilla Ring Attention, ensuring the algorithmic correctness in Attention computation.
The third one corresponds to the <span id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Chunk Placement Strategy</span> of the vanilla Ring Attention, and affects the workload balance of each iteration.
Then, we demonstrate that <span id="S3.SS2.SSS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Ring AllGather</span> can be decomposed into Multi-Ring AllGather while satisfying the first two properties (See Section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS2" title="3.2.2 Multi-Ring AllGather ‣ 3.2 Decomposition of Ring AllGather ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.2</span></a>).
Lastly, the chunk placement strategies for Ring Attention (Striped Attention and Zig-zag Ring Attention) cannot be directly ported to TASP. Thus, we present a Zig-zag chunk placement strategy for perfect load-balance (See Section <a href="#S3.SS2.SSS3" title="3.2.3 Zig-zag Chunk Placement for TASP ‣ 3.2 Decomposition of Ring AllGather ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2.3</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.2 </span>Multi-Ring AllGather</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As shown in Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.1.3 Multi-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, compared to the original Ring AllGather primitive that only assigns one query chunk for each accelerator, an <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-ring Multi-Ring AllGather communication primitive assigns <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> query chunks for each accelerator and designates a specific ring-styled data transfer for each query chunk.
The number of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> can be chosen arbitrarily, as long as the original query can be evenly split into <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> query chunks. The ring-style data transfer for each query chunk can also be designed arbitrarily and mutually different.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Since it is shown in the previous section that the topology of modern accelerators can be decomposed into a set of mutually orthogonal ring datapaths, we can thus design a Multi-Ring AllGather communication primitive 100%-percent align with a topology decomposition. For example, we present a <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math>-ring Multi-Ring AllGather Communication specifically designed for <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{8}-decomposition" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mn>8</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{8}-decomposition</annotation></semantics></math> of an 8-accelerator AlltoAll topology in Figure <a href="#S3.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ 3.1.3 Multi-Node topology Decomposition ‣ 3.1 Decomposition of Accelerator Topology ‣ 3 Design of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Full communication link utilization can be achieved if the ring-styled data transfer are 100%-percent align with the ring datapaths.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">However, to make sure this decomposition of Ring AllGather does not incur extra memory overhead or violate the algorithmic correctness of Attention calculation, we need to prove that it still adheres to the following properties:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Accessibility</span>: For any <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> tensor (assigned to accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) and any <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> tensor, since <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> tensor traverses all accelerators along its assigned ring-styled data transfer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> (a Hamiltonian cycle), it will eventually reach accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to attend to <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="KV_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KV_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> locally.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Zero-copy</span>: Each KV tensor is assigned to exactly one ring-styled data transfer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and is transferred solely along <math id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring only one copy exists at any time.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">3.2.3 </span>Zig-zag Chunk Placement for TASP</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The vanilla Ring Attention adopts a naive chunk placement strategy:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t[i]=KV[\frac{iS}{n},\frac{(i+1)S}{n})\;\text{(S is sequence length)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>(S is sequence length)</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t[i]=KV[\frac{iS}{n},\frac{(i+1)S}{n})\;\text{(S is sequence length)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Translating into plain text, this strategy first evenly splits all the KV tensors into <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> continuous blocks and map each block to accelerator, given <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> accelerators.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">However, when a causal mask is used, the naive chunk placement strategy will disrupt computation load balance. If the naive chunk placement strategy is used together with causal masking, <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> accelerators will become idle while only <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-i</annotation></semantics></math> accelerators perform computation at the <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration. In contrast, the Zig-Zag chunk placement strategy of Megatron CP ensures that all accelerators perform an equal amount of computation at each iteration, through a more complicated mapping:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E4X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle t[i]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle t[i]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle KV\left[\frac{iS}{2n},\frac{(i+1)S}{2n}\right)\cup" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo>∪</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle KV\left[\frac{iS}{2n},\frac{(i+1)S}{2n}\right)\cup</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E4Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E4Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle KV\left[\frac{(2n-i-1)S}{2n},\frac{(2n-i)S}{2n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>V</mi><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle KV\left[\frac{(2n-i-1)S}{2n},\frac{(2n-i)S}{2n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For perfectly load-balanced causal Attention computation, the Zig-zag chunk placement for Zig-zag Attention cannot be directly utilized in TASP. However, via some necessary adjustments, similar strategy can also be derived.
<span id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Zig-zag TASP:</span> Each KV chunk <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t[i,j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t[i,j]</annotation></semantics></math> assigned at accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math> and circulated via ring-style data transfer <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is further split into two parts:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t[i,j][0]=KV[\frac{(2nj+i)S}{2n(n-1)},\frac{(2nj+i+1)S}{2n(n-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t[i,j][0]=KV[\frac{(2nj+i)S}{2n(n-1)},\frac{(2nj+i+1)S}{2n(n-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="t[i,j][1]=KV[S-\frac{(2nj+i+1)S}{2n(n-1)},S-\frac{(2nj+i)S}{2n(n-1)})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t[i,j][1]=KV[S-\frac{(2nj+i+1)S}{2n(n-1)},S-\frac{(2nj+i)S}{2n(n-1)})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of the perfect load-balance of Zig-zag TASP is as follows:
Suppose for some accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, at some iteration <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="iter_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">iter_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, it receives KV chunks <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math> initially placed at accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> via some ring data-path <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> while at the same time the Q chunks <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>) are kept at <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&lt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&lt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the token indices of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>) are larger than those of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> but smaller than those of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math>, making only <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> needs to be attended, which is half of the transferred KV tensors via <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. On the contrary, if <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j&gt;r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j&gt;r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the token indices of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>) are smaller than both of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math> while those of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>) are larger than both of <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][0]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>j</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{KV}[i_{0},j_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math>, making only <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t_{Q}[i,r_{0}][1]</annotation></semantics></math> (<math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\forall i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall i</annotation></semantics></math>) needs to be attended, which is half of the query tokens. As a result, for any accelerator <math id="S3.SS2.SSS3.p4.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, its computation load at any iteration is the same, leading to 100% load-balance.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Implementation of TASP</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The implementation of TASP leverages two key techniques: (1) the use of AlltoAll collective communication for concurrent data transmission across multiple ring datapaths, and (2) pre-computed routing tables to minimize CPU scheduling overhead.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Pre-Computed Routing Tables</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To minimize CPU overhead during the distributed Attention computation, TASP pre-computes all routing tables before the forward pass. The <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">cal_in/out_mapping</span> functions as described in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4.1 Pre-Computed Routing Tables ‣ 4 Implementation of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> generate source and destination mappings for each send/receive based on a given topology decomposition scheme, eliminating the need for dynamic routing during the compute-intensive attention.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Calculate In/Out Mapping</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Looping matrix <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="looping[m][n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">looping[m][n]</annotation></semantics></math> direction <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\in\{+1,-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\in\{+1,-1\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             Mapping matrix <math id="alg2.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mapping[n][n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mapping[n][n]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mapping" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mapping</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> matrix filled with <math id="alg2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=0</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\leftarrow looping[i][j]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\leftarrow looping[i][j]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\leftarrow looping[i][(j+d)\bmod n]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\leftarrow looping[i][(j+d)\bmod n]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mapping[u][v]\leftarrow i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mapping[u][v]\leftarrow i</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg2.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg2.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="mapping" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">mapping</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Concurrent Ring-styled Data Transfer via AlltoAll</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike Ring Attention’s utilization of batched <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">sendRecv</span> collective, TASP can utilize a single <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AlltoAll</span> collective operation to simultaneously transmit KV blocks across all active ring datapaths (this optimization is for <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{m\times u}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{m\times u}</annotation></semantics></math>-decomposition scheme only). This approach fully leverages the low-level optimization for <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">AlltoAll</span> collective implemented in the Communication Collectives Libraries (NCCL and RCCL).</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The entire forward pass of TASP is illustrated in Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ 4.2 Concurrent Ring-styled Data Transfer via AlltoAll ‣ 4 Implementation of TASP ‣ TASP: Topology-aware Sequence Parallelism" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, where each accelerator prepares send buffers according to a pre-computed routing table and receives corresponding KV blocks from all other accelerators in each iteration.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> TASP Forward Pass</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg3.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="alg3.l0.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">process_group</span>, <span id="alg3.l0.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">world_size</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg3.l0a.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">out</span>, <span id="alg3.l0a.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lse</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             // Initialize routing tables: <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="looping\leftarrow gen\_hamilton\_circle(world\_size)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">looping\leftarrow gen\_hamilton\_circle(world\_size)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{out\_mapping}\leftarrow\texttt{cal\_out\_mapping}(\textit{looping})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">out_mapping</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">cal_out_mapping</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">looping</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{out\_mapping}\leftarrow\texttt{cal\_out\_mapping}(\textit{looping})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{in\_mapping}\leftarrow\texttt{cal\_in\_mapping}(\textit{looping})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">in_mapping</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">cal_in_mapping</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">looping</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{in\_mapping}\leftarrow\texttt{cal\_in\_mapping}(\textit{looping})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
             <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{para\_size}\leftarrow\textit{world\_size}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">para_size</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">world_size</mtext><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{para\_size}\leftarrow\textit{world\_size}-1</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
             // Stack KV tensors: <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textit{this\_kv}\leftarrow\left[\textit{stack}(k[i],v[i])\ \forall i\in\{0,\textit{para\_size}\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">stack</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">para_size</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{this\_kv}\leftarrow\left[\textit{stack}(k[i],v[i])\ \forall i\in\{0,\textit{para\_size}\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
             // Initialize receive buffers: <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\textit{next\_kv}\leftarrow\left[\textit{empty\_like}(\textit{this\_kv}[0])\ \forall i\in\{0,\textit{para\_size}\}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">next_kv</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">empty_like</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">para_size</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{next\_kv}\leftarrow\left[\textit{empty\_like}(\textit{this\_kv}[0])\ \forall i\in\{0,\textit{para\_size}\}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg3.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{step}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">step</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{step}=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">to</span> <math id="alg3.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{world\_size}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">world_size</mtext><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{world\_size}-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              // Extract K, V: <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\leftarrow\left[\textit{this\_kv}[i][0]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\leftarrow\left[\textit{this\_kv}[i][0]\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\leftarrow\left[\textit{this\_kv}[i][1]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\leftarrow\left[\textit{this\_kv}[i][1]\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{step}&lt;\textit{world\_size}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">step</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">world_size</mtext><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{step}&lt;\textit{world\_size}-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
               // Prepare send/recv buffers using routing tables:

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{send\_buf}\leftarrow\left[\textit{this\_kv}[\textit{out\_mapping}[i]]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">send_buf</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">out_mapping</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{send\_buf}\leftarrow\left[\textit{this\_kv}[\textit{out\_mapping}[i]]\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{recv\_buf}\leftarrow\left[\textit{next\_kv}[\textit{in\_mapping}[i]]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">recv_buf</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">next_kv</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">in_mapping</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>i</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{recv\_buf}\leftarrow\left[\textit{next\_kv}[\textit{in\_mapping}[i]]\right]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">13:</span>
              
              
               <span id="alg3.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">All-to-All</span>(<span id="alg3.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">send_buf</span>, <span id="alg3.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">recv_buf</span>)

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">14:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">15:</span>
              
              
              // Concatenate KV blocks: <math id="alg3.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\text{cat}}\leftarrow\textit{concat}(k,\text{dim}=\textit{seqlen})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>cat</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>dim</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">seqlen</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\text{cat}}\leftarrow\textit{concat}(k,\text{dim}=\textit{seqlen})</annotation></semantics></math><math id="alg3.l15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\text{cat}}\leftarrow\textit{concat}(v,\text{dim}=\textit{seqlen})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>cat</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">concat</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext>dim</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">seqlen</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\text{cat}}\leftarrow\textit{concat}(v,\text{dim}=\textit{seqlen})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">16:</span>
              
              
              // Compute Attention: <math id="alg3.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{output},\textit{lse\_curr}\leftarrow\texttt{flash\_attn}(q,k_{\text{cat}},v_{\text{cat}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">output</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">lse_curr</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">flash_attn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mtext>cat</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mtext>cat</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{output},\textit{lse\_curr}\leftarrow\texttt{flash\_attn}(q,k_{\text{cat}},v_{\text{cat}})</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="alg3.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{out},\textit{lse}\leftarrow\texttt{update\_out\_lse}(\textit{out},\textit{lse},\textit{output},\textit{lse\_curr})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">out</mtext><mo>,</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">lse</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">update_out_lse</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">out</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">lse</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">output</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">lse_curr</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{out},\textit{lse}\leftarrow\texttt{update\_out\_lse}(\textit{out},\textit{lse},\textit{output},\textit{lse\_curr})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">17:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{step}&lt;\textit{world\_size}-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">step</mtext><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">world_size</mtext><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{step}&lt;\textit{world\_size}-1</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">18:</span>
              
              
               // <span id="alg3.l18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Wait</span> for communication completion

</div>
<div id="alg3.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">19:</span>
              
              
               <math id="alg3.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{this\_kv}\leftarrow\textit{next\_kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">next_kv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{this\_kv}\leftarrow\textit{next\_kv}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg3.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{next\_kv}\leftarrow\textit{this\_kv}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">next_kv</mtext><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">this_kv</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{next\_kv}\leftarrow\textit{this\_kv}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">20:</span>
              
              
              <span id="alg3.l20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">21:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg3.l21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">22:</span>
              
              
             <span id="alg3.l22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg3.l22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textit{out},\textit{lse}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">out</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">lse</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textit{out},\textit{lse}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Evaluation</h2>

<figure id="S5.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S5.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.26541v1/NV-1-full.svg" id="S5.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/283;" width="476" height="283"></object>
